  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference1">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P13196 ALAS1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALAS1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALAS3</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">ALASH</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">OK/SW-cl.121</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref22" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Catalyzes the pyridoxal 5'-phosphate (PLP)-dependent condensation of succinyl-CoA and glycine to form aminolevulinic acid (ALA), with CoA and CO2 as by-products.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY succinyl-CoA + glycine + H(+) = 5-aminolevulinate + CO2 + CoACOFACTOR Activity increases about 2-fold over 72 hours of hypoxia compared with normoxia (PubMed:16234850). Activity increases in the presence of phenobarbital, chenodeoxycholic and NR1H4/FXR-specific agonist GW4064 (PubMed:17975826).PATHWAY Porphyrin-containing compound metabolism; protoporphyrin-IX biosynthesis; 5-aminolevulinate from glycine: step 1/1.SUBUNIT Homodimer (By similarity). Interacts (hydroxylated form) with VHL (PubMed:16234850).INTERACTION Localizes to the matrix side of the mitochondrion inner membrane.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS Up-regulated by bile acids; chenodeoxycholic acid, ursodeoxycholic acid and lithocholic acid and by the NR1H4/FXR-specific agonist GW4064.PTM In normoxia, is hydroxylated at Pro-576, promoting interaction with VHL, initiating ubiquitination and subsequent degradation via the proteasome.PTM Ubiquitinated; in normoxia following hydroxylation and interaction with VHL, leading to its subsequent degradation via the proteasome.SIMILARITY Belongs to the class-II pyridoxal-phosphate-dependent aminotransferase family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
